E(75,"Las Vegas Souvenir & Resort Gift Show 2026|Brick Loot","Brick Loot","Brand direct, flat year, minifigure pack carries a third; catalog not scaling","Brand direct 100%; monthly rev ~$43k; 12M MoM +4.7%; 8,264 reviews; top ASIN minifigure pack ~$12.5k/mo","Brick Loot on Amazon",f"""{H}

{LV}

From what we can see, Brick Loot does roughly $40k a month on Amazon, sold direct, with over 8,000 reviews across about 36 listings. The random minifigure pack is close to a third of it and the Titanic sets most of the rest. Growth over the last year is basically flat, which with that review base usually means the ads and content are not being pushed.

{CO}

Is it worth a short call ahead of Q4?

Yoni""",brand_sellers=["Brick Loot - Fast FREE Shipping from the USA"]),
E(76,"Las Vegas Souvenir & Resort Gift Show 2026|Active COCO","Active COCO","One live listing, very few reviews, sharp seasonal drop; early-stage channel","Brand direct 100%; monthly rev ~$40k; 1 active ASIN; 140 reviews; avg rating 4.2; MoM -28%","Active COCO on Amazon",f"""{H}

{LV}

From what we can see, Active COCO is doing roughly $40k a month on Amazon off a single live listing, the pre swim spray, sold direct. That is a good number for one product with only about 140 reviews. Last month was down close to 30% with the season, and at that review count the listing depends heavily on ads to hold rank through the winter.

{LAUNCH}

Open to a short call on the off-season and the review side?

Yoni""",brand_sellers=["Active CoCo"]),
E(77,"Las Vegas Souvenir & Resort Gift Show 2026|GeoToys","Geotoys","Growing fast through a single seller account; thin reviews for the catalog","Lidianas 100% on 82 offers (treated as brand's own account); monthly rev ~$40k; MoM +52%; 12M MoM +34%; 3,594 reviews","GeoPuzzle on Amazon",f"""{H}

{LV}

From what we can see, GeoToys does roughly $40k a month on Amazon through a single seller account, up sharply last month and over the last year. The GeoPuzzle sets carry it. The whole catalog of about 80 listings sits on around 3,600 reviews though, so the growth is still leaning on ads rather than on rank, and that is the moment to lock it in before Q4.

{CO}

Would it make sense to have a quick conversation?

Yoni""",brand_sellers=["Lidianas"],qa=["seller 'Lidianas' (82 offers, 100%) assumed to be GeoToys' own account; SmartScout single seller field shows 'Zoe's Toys'; verify"]),
E(78,"FNCE 2025|Just Better Brands","just better.","Single-product brand direct with modest growth; Subscribe & Save and ads angle","Brand direct 100%; monthly rev ~$36k; 3 listings; 1,684 reviews; avg rating 4.4; 12M MoM +9%","just better. fiber on Amazon",f"""{H}

{FN.format(b='Just Better')}

From what we can see, just better. does roughly $35k a month on Amazon, sold direct, across three sizes of the same fiber powder with about 1,700 reviews. Growth over the last year is in the single digits. For a daily-use product at $40 a tub, that usually means Subscribe & Save and the gut health search terms are not being worked as hard as they could be.

{CO}

Open to a short call?

Yoni""",brand_sellers=["JUST BETTER BRANDS"]),
E(79,"Las Vegas Souvenir & Resort Gift Show 2026|Huckleberry Haven, Inc","Huckleberry Haven","No brand account; ~100% via third-party resellers (MetaRetail, Artisan Owl, Zentra)","MetaRetail 28.7%; Artisan Owl 25.0%; Zentra 12.7%; brand direct 0%; monthly rev ~$33k; 4,077 reviews","Who sells Huckleberry Haven on Amazon",f"""{H}

{LV}

Looking at your listings, Huckleberry Haven products do roughly $33k a month on Amazon, and all of it is sold by third parties. MetaRetail and Artisan Owl are about a quarter each, with a handful of smaller resellers behind them, and we don't see a Huckleberry Haven account at all. So the pricing, the content and the reviews on the jam and licorice are being built by other people.

{CO}

Would it make sense to talk about taking that back?

Yoni"""),
